<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n89635" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόσκομμα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>,
			τό, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προσκόπτω</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>stumble</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λίθου πρόσκομμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>Is.</u>
					8.14
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ λίθος τοῦ π</span>. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ep.Rom.</u>
				9.33
			</span></i>: hence, <i>offence, obstacle, hindrance</i>, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ex.</u>
				23.33
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ep.Rom.</u>
				14.13
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>result of stumbling, bruise, hurt</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προσκομμάτων ἀπόλυσις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.1048c
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				3.97f
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
